# Compose entry point: HTTPS and HTTP/2 in front of the application. A real domain gets a public
# certificate; `localhost` gets a certificate from Caddy's local authority. The browser cache
# follows each open conversation through a connection that stays open, and HTTP/1.1 allows only
# 6 of them per origin: over HTTP/2, they share a single connection.

# The guest chat component (`/embed/`) loads as a module, with its parts and fonts, from the pages
# of other sites: its files hold no data, so any site may read them.

{$WICA_DOMAIN:localhost} {
	header /embed/* Access-Control-Allow-Origin "*"
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}
